/*  table05 -- A TABLE PIN READS THE FILE OF THE DICTIONARY THAT DECLARES IT
    (DEV.md 4c C398 slice (c), review row TG-02).

        feedA -> [ A: pipe P1 ] -> outA
        feedB -> [ B: pipe P1 ] -> outB

    Each sector keeps its own property dictionary (sectors/<S>/constant/
    thermoPhysPropDict, inheriting the plant's) and pins water's liquid
    viscosity to `table crcWaterMu` -- the SAME pin text in both.  Each
    sector holds its own constant/experiments/crcWaterMu.dat: sector A the
    eleven evaluated points of the handbook table, sector B every second of
    them (six points, 20 K apart).  At 300 K (between the 20 and 30 degC
    points of A, and the 20 and 40 degC points of B) the two interpolants
    differ, so each pipe's viscosity, Reynolds number and friction show
    which file its sector read.  The plant's own constant/experiments/ holds
    a DECOY of the same name with every value doubled: no sector may read it
    (there is no walk up the folders), and the golden master would show it
    if one did.

    The two sectors' packages are told apart by their identity, which
    carries each table's own text and file (review row TG-15). */

sectors
(
    A
    B
);

connections
{
    feedA   { to A/feed; }
    feedB   { to B/feed; }
    outA    { from A/downstream; }
    outB    { from B/downstream; }
}

reports
{
    streamTable    { }
    massBalance    { }
    energyBalance  { }
}
